Edinburgh</source><year>2004</year></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>ISD Scotland</collab></person-group><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.isdscotland.org/deprivation"/></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Murray</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Graham</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Dlugolecka</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>How many general practitioners for 1433 patients</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>1995</year><volume>310</volume><fpage>1072</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greenland</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ecological versus individual-level sources of bias in ecologic estimates of contextual health effects</article-title><source>Int J Epidemiology</source><year>2001</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>1343</fpage><lpage>50</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/ije/30.6.1343</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>GD</given-names></name><name><surname>Hart</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Watt</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Hole</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Hawthorne</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Individual social class, area-based deprivation, cardiovascular disease risk factors, and mortality: the renfrew and paisley study</article-title><source>J Epidemiol Community Health</source><year>1998</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>399</fpage><lpage>405</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9764262</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pearce</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The ecological fallacy strikes back</article-title><source>J Epidemiol Community Health</source><year>2000</year><volume>54</volume><fpage>326</fpage><lpage>327</lpage><comment>doi: 10.1136/jech.54.5.326</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10814650</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/jech.54.5.326</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>ISD Scotland</collab></person-group><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.isdscotland.org/pti"/></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Doran</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Fullwood</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Gravelle</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Reeves</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kontopantelis</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Hiroeh</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Roland</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pay-for-performance programs in family practices in the United Kingdom</article-title><source>New England Journal of Medicine</source><year>2006</year><volume>355</volume><fpage>375</fpage><lpage>384</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16870916</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1056/NEJMsa055505</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>